  "scope": "Share low-digit replacement invariant in window digit proofs",
  "validation": "Paired target and ArithmeticWindowBits builds pass with identical client objects. Fresh ArithmeticRepunit and prior source-current BinaryPopulation/BinaryCarry providers are recorded. All 51 existing target declaration/type/axiom reports match, one private helper is added, and 28,973 default simp and 13,172 instance entries match.",
  "limitations": [
    "ArithmeticCyclicWord and ArithmeticMaskConstants also directly import the target and were not rebuilt. Target-pinned probes do not cover every environment extension or all downstream clients.",
    "The earlier unrestricted rewrite v2 failed because it also rewrote the quotient on the right; its source/log/time are retained without contemporaneous input/output hash receipts. The v1 and v3 provisional evidence is also historical; their original output object path was overwritten and they are not the paired evidence.",
    "The prior BinaryPopulation build receipt does not pin its own Foundation/Mathlib direct inputs. Other transitive project and package inputs remain cached; no full current-source closure build is established.",
    "One shared-load timing pair is not a general performance benchmark. Compiled objects are not included in the ZIP; object hashes and first-provider resolution are retained in receipts, and external objects are required for independent byte checks."
  ],
